# .starcistacks custody: the ordered modules/schemas/stacks-layout.yaml custody.gitignoreRules, plus the
# value-free members this kit tracks (seeds, rendered environment.json and the VPS stack file).
# Decrypted materializations and the demo age identity are never tracked.
.starcistacks/**
!.starcistacks/**/
!.starcistacks/**/KEYS.md
!.starcistacks/**/.gitkeep
!.starcistacks/application-stacks.yaml
!.starcistacks/*/README.md
!.starcistacks/*/environment.json
!.starcistacks/*/seeds/**
!.starcistacks/*/infra/stack.yaml
!.starcistacks/*/infra/compose/**
!.starcistacks/*/infra/terraform/**
.starcistacks/*/infra/**/.env
.starcistacks/*/infra/**/.env.*
.starcistacks/*/infra/**/*.env
.starcistacks/*/infra/**/*.key
.starcistacks/*/infra/**/*.pem
.starcistacks/*/infra/**/*.tfvars
.starcistacks/*/infra/terraform/.terraform/
.starcistacks/*/infra/terraform/*.tfstate
.starcistacks/*/infra/terraform/*.tfstate.*
.starcistacks/*/infra/terraform/files/
.starcistacks/*/infra/terraform/*.tar.gz
!.starcistacks/**/*.enc

# UAT run videos ARE tracked, by owner ruling (2026-09-18): the recording is acceptance evidence an
# outsourcer has to be able to open from a fresh clone, and
# scripts/check-example-work.mjs's concept 12 refuses a `done` uat-flow whose settled run has no
# `videos/` with at least one playable recording in it — so a rule that keeps the .webm out of Git makes
# the gate unsatisfiable by construction on any clone. The run's manifest.yaml carries each video's
# sha256, which is now an integrity check on a file that is actually present rather than a pointer to a
# byte nobody can retrieve. Screens (PNG) stay tracked, same as every other capture in this tree.
